// Squads move on after taking a flag (crates/game_server/src/ai/strategy.rs): on Gulf of Oman
// (16) the US squads walk from the Beachhead to the neutral Village (10, 33, 136) and take
// it. A squad mostly at a flag its team takes (or three of it) gets its next order in the
// tick the flag changes hands ("ai flow: ... new order": the commander plans at once) and
// most of it leaves ("squad moved off": no more than a third of its members within the flag's
// radius plus 40 m, not counting the one or two left to guard it while enemies are about).
// Fails if nobody takes the Village within 180 s, if no such squad gets an order elsewhere
// within 60 s after that, or if it doesn't move off within 60 s. The server log's `ai flow:`
// lines say what every squad did after a capture (`still there 15 s after its new order:
// ...` lists what keeps one).
// client --scenario scenarios/ai/capture_flow.ron --out target/scenarios/ai/capture_flow
(
    level: "gulf_of_oman",
    size: 16,
    bots: 16,
    spectate: true,
    steps: [
        WaitReady,
        ForbidLog("panicked"),
        // The Village from the north-east, 35 m off and 22 m up.
        Camera((35.0, 55.0, 161.0), 45.0, -32.0),
        Wait(8.0),
        Screenshot("approach"),
        ExpectLog("took Village", 180.0),
        Screenshot("taken"),
        ExpectLog("ago): new order", 60.0),
        Wait(6.0),
        Screenshot("moving_on"),
        ExpectLog("squad moved off", 60.0),
        Screenshot("moved_off"),
        // Wider, from higher up: the squad on its way to the next flag.
        Camera((110.0, 130.0, 236.0), 45.0, -38.0),
        Wait(5.0),
        Screenshot("overview"),
        Quit,
    ],
)
